<h2 id="categories"><span class="sec-mark" aria-hidden="true">§ I</span> Categories</h2>

<p class="sec-lead">If these counts and the real total ever drift apart, <code class="tok">audit-baseline</code> fails the build. There are {{ roster.skillCategoryCount }} categories, assigned by hand rather than derived from disk. That is why they live beside the deriver, and why this section can give you counts without a per-skill grouping.</p>

<div class="grid-rule grid-3 lane-grid">
  {% for name, n in roster.skillCategories %}
  <div class="cell">
    <div class="cell-kicker">{{ name }}</div>
    <p>{{ n }}</p>
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
</div>

<h2 id="roster"><span class="sec-mark" aria-hidden="true">§ II</span> The roster</h2>

<p class="sec-lead">{{ roster.skills | length }} baseline-owned skills, in alphabetical order. Each summary is excerpted from the first sentence of the skill's own description. It is never reworded, because a skill prompt is a contract and editing it from a template would quietly change how the skill behaves in a session (the roster derives from the files themselves).</p>

